Z||000000||AgaricX||11-14-2001||01:04 AM||||I have seen quite a few convertibles in the picture acrchives and on numerous sites.  There is NO dount that I will cut the top off my lovely (not) car before I get her painted.  But I've been thinking on and off about some things.<P>First... I see some that have no ragtop and they don't seem to have any way to attach one.  They have 2 "humps" behind each of the seats where the decklid wents are (were) Personally, I love the way those look as opposed to having the top sitting there.  Is there a kit or body pieces that can be bought for that?<P>Second... I want to seal my doors shut.  I have heard quite a few complaints about rattle and seeing the door vibrate when you're driving when the car has been x-braced.  I want none of that at all.  Not to mention I think It would absolutely look wonderful.  Hop in... hop out.  Dukes of hazard style.  I've thought about shaving the handles and thats just not enough for me.  As long as this is my "experiment" car (1st Fiero)  I might as well go whole hog.  Has anyone thought of this?  Am I nutzo?  I'm going to take some digipics (finally) of my work in progrss and photoshop them to see how they fly.  Can anyone see any major downsides to this?  C'mon... If youve got cronstructive criticism throw it my way.<P>Man I'm tired... and I still have hours of genome work to do.<P>*sigh*<BR><P>------------------<BR>85 SE 3800<BR>Body Work in Progress<BR>Pic to follow when it's not an eyesore.||||reg||7
