Z||000003||ChopTop||11-14-2001||09:11 AM||||The behind the seats humps cars you've have seen were Pontiac concept cars.  In fact, I think its the same car with new paint jobs and updated body panels.<BR>Another idea would be to (don't know if it's possible) but shorten the bottom of the doors by about four inches.  Then weld in additional bracing under the doors.  When you open the door you have too step over and drop down into the seats.  The new bracing then would be covered by modified body panels.<BR>A no hardtop car is possible, but you wouldn't want to travel too far.  You could have a tarp made than essential covers the interior.  A zipper could then be included over the drivers portion allowing driving if need be.  I know a lot of the old English sports cars had features like that.  Good luck if you do do it, take lots of pics!<P>BTW I think there is a forum member that has recently been advertising a x frame for sale.<p>[This message has been edited by ChopTop (edited 11-14-2001).]||||reg||1
